From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:03:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable the GPU

Enable the GPU at one fixed operating point, 1008 MHz on its own PLL with
VDD-GPU at 960 mV, and describe the GPU rail.

drm/imagination sets no clock rate and uses no regulator, so the board
has to pin both. Left alone, the GPU core clock comes out of reset on
PLL_GPU0 at the PLL's reset rate (840 MHz), while DCDC4 stays where the
boot chain left it (800 mV), which is below the vendor's voltage for that
frequency.

- Clock: PLL_GPU0 at 1008 MHz (N 84, P0 2, VCO 2016 MHz), the core clock
  on it undivided. 1008 MHz is the top row of the vendor's GPU OPP table
  and the only row this PLL reaches with its VCO in range.
- Rail: DCDC4 is VDD-GPU and feeds nothing else (schematic; DCDC4 is not
  paralleled with DCDC5 by the poly-phase bits). 960 mV is the highest
  voltage the vendor table gives 1008 MHz across all speed bins, and the
  top of the schematic's VDD-GPU range (0.8 V to 0.96 V). min == max,
  since there is no OPP table and nothing may move the rail. The ramp
  delay follows the AXP318W DCDC slew rate (7.8125 us per 10 mV step).

Ordering: the regulator core sets DCDC4 when the PMIC probes; the clock
rates are applied when the GPU driver probes. With DRM_POWERVR as a
module (defconfig) that is after the PMIC. Nothing in the device tree
enforces it for a built-in GPU driver, because the binding has no GPU
supply.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the core clock runs
from PLL_GPU0 at 1008 MHz (N 84, P0 2) undivided, vdd-gpu is enabled at
960 mV (DCDC4 code 0x2e), and the firmware boots. The GPU stays active
while idle with no client (open). No render job was submitted.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index fb15a32fa5f2..76793d350b30 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -122,6 +122,17 @@ ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 	};
 };
 
+&gpu {
+	/*
+	 * Fixed operating point: PLL_GPU0 at 1008 MHz (VCO 2016 MHz, P0 2)
+	 * with the core clock undivided, on VDD-GPU at 960 mV (DCDC4).
+	 */
+	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU0>, <&ccu CLK_GPU0>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU0>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <1008000000>, <1008000000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &mmc0 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sdmmc-3v3", "sdmmc-1v8";
 	pinctrl-1 = <&mmc0_3v3_pins>, <&mmc0_clk_pin>;
@@ -216,6 +227,15 @@ reg_dcdc3: dcdc3 {
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
+			/* GPU, fixed at the 1008 MHz operating point */
+			reg_dcdc4: dcdc4 {
+				regulator-name = "vdd-gpu";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <960000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <960000>;
+				regulator-ramp-delay = <1280>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
 			reg_dcdc5: dcdc5 {
 				regulator-name = "vdd-cpul";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
